Entries for the North Dakota QSO Party used by in-state stations
The 53 North Dakota counties (each its own multiplier), then the 50 states, DC and the rules' 13 Canadian abbreviations.
North Dakota itself is not a multiplier for an in-state entrant: the class refuses it (49 states excluding North Dakota).
DXCC countries count for points only, never as a multiplier, so there is no DX entry.
The 13 are the rules' own list (NY4I, 2026-11-20): AB BC LB MB NB NF NS NT ON PE QC SK YT.
Labrador (LB) and Newfoundland (NF) are TWO multipliers; the combined spelling NL is taken as Newfoundland.
Nunavut is not on the list: it was part of the Northwest Territories, so NU keeps its own QTH and counts as NT.
The provinces are written here, not taken from P13, which has no LB or NF and spells Newfoundland LA.
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.
https://ndarrlsection.com

INCLUDE FILE northdakota_cty.dom
INCLUDE FILE S50.DOM
INCLUDE FILE DC.DOM
Ab = VE6,AB,ALB,ALT,^Alberta
Bc = VE7,BC,^British Columbia
Lb = VO2,LB,LAB,^Labrador
Mb = VE4,MB,MAN,^Manitoba
Nb = VE9,NB,^New Brunswick
Nf = VO1,NF,NL,^Newfoundland
Ns = VE1,NS,^Nova Scotia
Nt = VE8,NT,NW,NWT,^Northwest Territory
On = VE3,ON,ONT,^Ontario
Pe = VY2,PE,PEI,^Prince Edward Is.
Qc = VE2,QC,QUE,QU,PQ,^Quebec
Sk = VE5,SK,SAS,SASK,^Saskatchewan
Yt = VY1,YT,YK,YU,^Yukon Territory
Nu > Nt = VY0,NU
